  "title": "Information and Media Permanent Secretary Thabo Kawana says the curre...",
  "description": "Information and Media Permanent Secretary Thabo Kawana says the current state of Victoria Falls is the worst, clearly highlighting the low water levels the country is facing, which is impacting power generation. Mr. Kawana has encouraged Zambians to heed the government's call to go green by planting trees. He told journalists in Livingstone that the current power deficit in the country is purely a climate change issue and has nothing to do with leadership. Meanwhile, Mr. Kawana reassured consumers that all the mealie meal on the market is safe for consumption and that there is no shortage of the commodity in any part of the country.",
